d":0.027892661984447308,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":42.1,"_gate_share_shrink":-0.03264182878499855,"_gp_share_shrink":true,"_score_share_shrink":90.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.0,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":0.0,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"Banco Santander, S.A. provides various financial products and services to individuals, small and medium-sized enterprises, large corporations, and public entities worldwide. The company operates through five segments: Retail & Commercial Banking, Digital Consumer Bank, Corporate & Investment Banking, Wealth Management & Insurance, and Payments. It offers demand and time deposits, mutual funds, and current and savings accounts; mortgages, consumer finance, loans, and various financing solutions; and project finance, debt capital markets, global transaction banking, and corporate finance services. The company also provides credit and debit cards, real estate loans, microfinance, and auto loans; corporate and investment banking services; advice on mergers and acquisitions; wealth, asset, and risk management services; and digital payments and technology solutions. In addition, it is involved in the securitization, leasing, management of portfolios, e-commerce, air transport, aircraft rental, software, consulting, fund and investment management, renewable energy, vehicle rental, insurance, advertising, marketing, telemarketing, automotive, agricultural, factoring, securities brokerage and investment, pension fund management, trade intermediary, venture capital fund, renting, restaurant, electricity production, IT, internet, and financial advisory and other activities; management, and other real estate activities; and purchase and sale of vehicles. Further, the company offers mobile and online banking services. Banco Santander, S.A. was formerly known as Banco Santander Central Hispano SA and changed its name to Banco Santander, S.A. in February 2007. The company was incorporated in 1856 and is headquartered in Madrid, Spain.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Hector Blas Grisi Checa | Group CEO & Executive Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $10.7M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 185K people.","financial_summary":["Banco Santander, S.A. Sponsored is a large-cap financial services business with a $169.3B market cap.","Returns on capital run at 153% against a 10% cost of capital \u2014 a 143-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The company is burning through $23.1B of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.1) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Financial Services peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Reinvestment rate supports 29% organic growth capacity \u2014 capital is compounding inside the business","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","ROIC sits in the top quartile of Financial Services peers \u2014 the moat is wider than the neighbourhood","Among the least levered in Financial Services \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"INVESTOR ALERT: Pomerantz Law Firm Investigates Claims On Behalf of Investors of Banco Santander, S.A. - SAN","source":"prnewswire.com","link":"https://www.prnewswire.com/news-releases/investor-alert-pomerantz-law-firm-investigates-claims-on-behalf-of-investors-of-banco-santander-sa---san-302931531.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793932020.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.447,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["legal"]},{"title":"Contrasting Southern Missouri Bancorp (NASDAQ:SMBC) & Banco Santander (NYSE:SAN)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/05/contrasting-southern-missouri-bancorp-nasdaqsmbc-banco-santander-nysesan.html","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793877343.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Vise Technologies Inc. Purchases 73,198 Shares of Banco Santander, S.A. $SAN","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/04/vise-technologies-